        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"thumbs up\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f44d\" role=\"img\" title=\"thumbs up\">:thumbs_up:</span> cfallin submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14464#pullrequestreview-5382412511\">PR review</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>These all look fine overall, thanks! Just one nit below.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 628434850,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1790872666
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> cfallin created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14464#discussion_r4157928604\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Let's put the constant on the right of the <code>+</code> in the RHS of the rewrite (so <code>(x - y) + (C1 - C2)</code>) -- this is the direction in which we canonicalize constants in general and should play better with other const-folding rules.</p>\n</blockquote>",
